    "best": "mobilenet_v3_large",
    "explanation": "**MobileNetV3** (MobileNetV3-Large (ImageNet, fine-tuned)) is recommended: it has the highest score (97.5% macro-F1, accuracy 97.5% on the held-out test set) and is also the fastest on the CPU of the models within 1 point of it. It takes 29.2 ms per image on the CPU (about 34 frames/s), fast enough for the live camera. It is also the most robust: its lowest macro-F1 in the corruption tests is 91% (noise). MobileNetV3 was designed for phones: depthwise-separable convolutions and squeeze-and-excitation give it the fewest multiply-adds of the three. By comparison, EfficientNet-B0 reaches 97.0% macro-F1 at 40.8 ms/img (1.4x slower on the CPU with 1.8x the multiply-adds, weaker under noise (73% vs 91% macro-F1)); ResNet-18 reaches 96.7% macro-F1 at 50.3 ms/img (1.7x slower on the CPU with 8.4x the multiply-adds). On a GPU the fastest is ResNet-18 (5.3 ms vs 8.6 ms), but the app must also run smoothly on laptops without one.",
